solnix: tzmon -- ThinkPad discrete-GPU power-off at boot, ON by default where it applies (opt out with
-B solnix-dgpu-off=0), the way Linux powers off a GPU that no driver owns.

WHY
- Measured on the X1 Extreme Gen5 (r1 image, plain boot, 2026-10-21): the RTX 3080 Ti (10de:2420 at 01:00.0,
  \_SB.PC00.PEG1.PEGP) idled in D0 with vgatext on 01:00.0 and audiohd on its HDMI audio 01:00.1. The EC's GPU
  sensor (tzmon:0:THM0:ec_gput) went 53 C -> 76 -> 83 -> 92-94 C in ten idle minutes, THM0 42 -> 67 C with the CPU
  at 400 MHz, then the machine powered off silently (the EC cutoff).
- Under Linux the same GPU runs NVIDIA's runtime D3, so it is powered off whenever idle. For a GPU with no driver
  Linux does pci_set_power_state(D3cold): the endpoint to D3hot through its PM capability, then the root port's D3
  power resource (_PR3) off, which the platform implements as link-down, reset and power-cut.

WHERE IT LIVES: in tzmon's ThinkPad shim, called from tzmon_attach right after the HKEY init.
- The gate is the ThinkPad HKEY that 0002 already finds (tzmon_hkey), and tzmon is force-attached early
  (tzmon.conf ddi-forceattach=1), before devfsadm.

WHAT THE X1E'S TABLES SAY (BIOS N3JET48W, SSDT14 "NvOptTbl", solnix-bank/evidence/x1e-acpi-N3JET48W/ssdt/SSDT14.dsl)
- \_SB.PC00.PEG1 has _PR0 = _PR3 = { PXP } (lines 550-557). Linux lists it as \_SB_.PC00.PEG1.PXP_ (LNXPOWER:01).
- PXP._OFF (lines 525-547) acts when OSYS > 0x07D9; illumos's _OSI answers make OSYS 0x07DF. It runs GC6I if
  PEGP.TDGC is 1, which only NVIDIA's _DSM (NGC6) sets; otherwise it runs POFF().
- POFF (lines 433-494) returns early if the port is empty or already off, saves the link state (NVPF), puts the
  link in L2/L3 ready (PEG1.DL23), drops the clock request (SPCO), asserts the GPU reset GPIO and cuts its power
  GPIO. So with no NVIDIA driver, PXP._OFF needs NO _DSM handshake. After it, config reads of 01:00.x return all
  1s, and nothing may touch the device again.

WHEN IT ACTS (all must hold; otherwise one console line, or silence off a ThinkPad, and nothing changes)
1. solnix-dgpu-off is not "0" (a -B string, or an int in tzmon.conf). Unset means ON.
2. The ThinkPad HKEY is present, and \_SB.PC00.PEG1 (or \_SB.PCI0.PEG1) exists. Without them, the default boot is
   SILENT (EC2, other machines); an explicit solnix-dgpu-off logs "not a ThinkPad dGPU".
3. The port's _PR3 package names a PowerResource object.
4. Among the root port's devinfo children there is a function with vendor-id 0x10de and class-code 0x03xxxx
   (display), read from the properties the PCI enumerator set, not from config space.
5. No function is the console framebuffer (fbdip). On the X1E the console is the iGPU (display@2).
6. Every function is unbound or bound to a generic driver: vgatext (display) or audiohd (HDMI audio). Any other
   driver (e.g. a future nvidia) means hands off.
7. The power resource's _STA is not 0.

THE SEQUENCE
- ndi_devi_offline every function. This detaches vgatext/audiohd if they attached (consconfig attaches display nodes
  while it looks for the console, so vgatext can be on 01:00.0 before tzmon runs), and an offline node is never
  attached again by devfsadm or a later bus_config (i_ddi_attachchild checks DEVI_IS_DEVICE_OFFLINE). If one
  function refuses, the ones already offlined are put back online and the GPU stays powered.
- Every function to D3hot via PMCSR, 10 ms, read back.
- The power resource's _OFF, then its _STA.
- One console line: port, function count, how many drivers were detached, the D3hot result, _STA before -> after.
After _OFF nothing reads or writes the GPU's config space.

--- a/usr/src/uts/i86pc/io/tzmon/tzmon.c
+++ b/usr/src/uts/i86pc/io/tzmon/tzmon.c
@@ -42,6 +42,11 @@
 #include <sys/acpica.h>
 #include <sys/sdt.h>
 #include <sys/kstat.h>
+#include <sys/pci.h>
+#include <sys/pci_cfgspace.h>
+#include <sys/sunndi.h>
+#include <sys/ddi_implfuncs.h>
+#include <sys/consdev.h>
 
 #include "tzmon.h"
 
@@ -94,6 +99,7 @@
 static void tzmon_hkey_disable(void);
 static void tzmon_kstat_create(thermal_zone_t *tzp, int instance);
 static void tzmon_ec_temps(int *t, int *l);
+static void tzmon_dgpu_off(dev_info_t *dip);
 
 extern void halt(char *);
 
@@ -202,6 +208,8 @@
 
 	/* before the zones are first evaluated; see tzmon_hkey_enable() */
 	tzmon_hkey_enable();
+	/* on by default on a ThinkPad dGPU, -B solnix-dgpu-off=0 opts out */
+	tzmon_dgpu_off(dip);
 	tzmon_find_zones();
 	mutex_enter(&zone_list_lock);
 	if (zone_count < 1) {
@@ -1059,3 +1067,279 @@
 	    tzmon_hkey_notify);
 	tzmon_hkey = NULL;
 }
+
+
+/*
+ * ThinkPad discrete-GPU power-off at boot: ON by default where it applies,
+ * opt out with -B solnix-dgpu-off=0.
+ *
+ * Under Linux the X1 Extreme Gen5's RTX 3080 Ti runs NVIDIA's runtime D3
+ * (fine-grained): the GPU is powered off whenever it is idle. Nothing drives
+ * it under illumos, so it idles in D0. Measured on that machine: the EC's GPU
+ * sensor (tzmon:0:THM0:ec_gput) went 53 -> 94 C in ten idle minutes, then the
+ * EC cut power. This does what Linux's pci_set_power_state(D3cold) does for a
+ * GPU with no driver: the endpoint to D3hot through its PCI PM capability,
+ * then the root port's D3 power resource (its _PR3) off, so the platform cuts
+ * the GPU's power.
+ *
+ * The X1E's tables (BIOS N3JET48W, SSDT14 "NvOptTbl"): \_SB.PC00.PEG1 has
+ * _PR0 = _PR3 = { PXP } (SSDT14.dsl lines 550-557). PXP._OFF (lines 525-547)
+ * runs POFF() (lines 433-494) unless PEGP.TDGC is set, and only the NVIDIA
+ * _DSM sets TDGC. POFF returns early if the port is empty or already off,
+ * then saves link state (NVPF), puts the link in L2/L3 ready (PEG1.DL23),
+ * drops the clock request, asserts the GPU reset GPIO and cuts its power GPIO.
+ * With no NVIDIA driver loaded, that needs no _DSM handshake. After it the
+ * GPU's config space reads all 1s, so nothing here touches it again, and its
+ * functions stay offline so no driver attaches to them later.
+ *
+ * Applies only when ALL of these hold; anything else does nothing:
+ * - the ThinkPad HKEY (tzmon_hkey);
+ * - \_SB.PC00.PEG1 (or \_SB.PCI0.PEG1) whose _PR3 names a power resource;
+ * - a function under it that is display class (0x03) from vendor 0x10de, read
+ *   from the devinfo properties the PCI enumerator set (no config access);
+ * - no function is the console framebuffer (fbdip);
+ * - every function is unbound, or bound to a generic driver: vgatext (display)
+ *   or audiohd (the GPU's HDMI audio). Any other driver means hands off.
+ * vgatext/audiohd can attach before tzmon's force-attach (consconfig attaches
+ * display nodes while it looks for the console), so a bound generic driver is
+ * detached by ndi_devi_offline, which also keeps devfsadm from re-attaching.
+ *
+ * Without the HKEY (EC2, QEMU without the test SSDT, other laptops) it is
+ * silent unless the opt-out was given, so a non-ThinkPad console is unchanged.
+ */
+static char *tzmon_dgpu_ports[] = { "\\_SB.PC00.PEG1", "\\_SB.PCI0.PEG1",
+	NULL };
+/* the only drivers this may detach from the dGPU's functions */
+static char *tzmon_dgpu_generic[] = { "vgatext", "audiohd", NULL };
+
+#define	TZMON_DGPU_VENDOR	0x10de
+#define	TZMON_DGPU_MAXFN	8
+
+typedef struct tzmon_dgpu_fn {
+	dev_info_t	*dip;
+	int		bus, dev, func;
+	int		class;
+	const char	*drv;		/* bound driver, NULL if none attached */
+} tzmon_dgpu_fn_t;
+
+/* Put one function in D3hot via its PCI PM capability; -1 if it has none. */
+static int
+tzmon_dgpu_d3hot(tzmon_dgpu_fn_t *fn)
+{
+	uint8_t ptr;
+	uint16_t pmcsr;
+	int n;
+
+	if (!((*pci_getw_func)(fn->bus, fn->dev, fn->func, PCI_CONF_STAT) &
+	    PCI_STAT_CAP))
+		return (-1);
+	ptr = (*pci_getb_func)(fn->bus, fn->dev, fn->func, PCI_CONF_CAP_PTR);
+	for (n = 0; ptr >= 0x40 && n < 48; n++) {
+		ptr &= ~3;
+		if ((*pci_getb_func)(fn->bus, fn->dev, fn->func, ptr) ==
+		    PCI_CAP_ID_PM)
+			break;
+		ptr = (*pci_getb_func)(fn->bus, fn->dev, fn->func, ptr + 1);
+	}
+	if (ptr < 0x40 || n >= 48)
+		return (-1);
+	pmcsr = (*pci_getw_func)(fn->bus, fn->dev, fn->func, ptr + PCI_PMCSR);
+	pmcsr = (pmcsr & ~PCI_PMCSR_STATE_MASK) | PCI_PMCSR_D3HOT;
+	(*pci_putw_func)(fn->bus, fn->dev, fn->func, ptr + PCI_PMCSR, pmcsr);
+	/* PCIe: 10 ms from D0 to D3hot before the next access */
+	delay(drv_usectohz(10000));
+	pmcsr = (*pci_getw_func)(fn->bus, fn->dev, fn->func, ptr + PCI_PMCSR);
+	return (pmcsr & PCI_PMCSR_STATE_MASK);
+}
+
+/*
+ * The opt-out: -B solnix-dgpu-off=0 (a boot property: a string) or
+ * solnix-dgpu-off=0; in tzmon.conf (an int). Looked up from tzmon's node up
+ * to the root node. Returns 1 (default), 0 (opted out); *given says whether
+ * the property was set at all.
+ */
+static int
+tzmon_dgpu_wanted(dev_info_t *dip, int *given)
+{
+	char *s;
+	int v;
+
+	*given = 1;
+	if (ddi_prop_lookup_string(DDI_DEV_T_ANY, dip, 0, "solnix-dgpu-off",
+	    &s) == DDI_PROP_SUCCESS) {
+		v = (strcmp(s, "0") != 0);
+		ddi_prop_free(s);
+		return (v);
+	}
+	/* not set anywhere (-1): on by default */
+	v = ddi_prop_get_int(DDI_DEV_T_ANY, dip, 0, "solnix-dgpu-off", -1);
+	*given = (v != -1);
+	return (v != 0);
+}
+
+static boolean_t
+tzmon_dgpu_is_generic(const char *drv)
+{
+	int i;
+
+	for (i = 0; tzmon_dgpu_generic[i] != NULL; i++)
+		if (strcmp(drv, tzmon_dgpu_generic[i]) == 0)
+			return (B_TRUE);
+	return (B_FALSE);
+}
+
+static void
+tzmon_dgpu_off(dev_info_t *dip)
+{
+	ACPI_HANDLE port = NULL, pr = NULL;
+	ACPI_BUFFER rb;
+	ACPI_OBJECT *pkg;
+	dev_info_t *pdip = NULL, *cdip;
+	tzmon_dgpu_fn_t fn[TZMON_DGPU_MAXFN];
+	char *name = NULL;
+	int nfn = 0, sta0 = -1, sta1 = -1, i, d3[TZMON_DGPU_MAXFN], given;
+	int nvdisp = 0, ndet = 0, wanted;
+	ACPI_OBJECT_TYPE t;
+
+	wanted = tzmon_dgpu_wanted(dip, &given);
+	for (i = 0; tzmon_dgpu_ports[i] != NULL && port == NULL; i++) {
+		if (AcpiGetHandle(NULL, tzmon_dgpu_ports[i], &port) != AE_OK)
+			port = NULL;
+		else
+			name = tzmon_dgpu_ports[i];
+	}
+	if (tzmon_hkey == NULL || port == NULL) {
+		/* the default case off ThinkPads: say nothing */
+		if (given)
+			cmn_err(CE_NOTE, "tzmon: solnix-dgpu-off: not a "
+			    "ThinkPad dGPU (%s); nothing done",
+			    tzmon_hkey == NULL ? "no HKEY" :
+			    "no PEG1 root port");
+		return;
+	}
+	if (!wanted) {
+		cmn_err(CE_NOTE, "tzmon: solnix-dgpu-off=0: %s: discrete GPU "
+		    "left powered", name);
+		return;
+	}
+
+	/* the D3 power resource: the first entry of the port's _PR3 */
+	rb.Length = ACPI_ALLOCATE_BUFFER;
+	rb.Pointer = NULL;
+	if (AcpiEvaluateObjectTyped(port, "_PR3", NULL, &rb,
+	    ACPI_TYPE_PACKAGE) == AE_OK) {
+		pkg = rb.Pointer;
+		if (pkg->Package.Count >= 1 &&
+		    pkg->Package.Elements[0].Type == ACPI_TYPE_LOCAL_REFERENCE &&
+		    AcpiGetType(pkg->Package.Elements[0].Reference.Handle,
+		    &t) == AE_OK && t == ACPI_TYPE_POWER)
+			pr = pkg->Package.Elements[0].Reference.Handle;
+		AcpiOsFree(rb.Pointer);
+	}
+	if (pr == NULL) {
+		cmn_err(CE_NOTE, "tzmon: solnix-dgpu-off: %s has no _PR3 "
+		    "power resource; nothing done", name);
+		return;
+	}
+
+	/*
+	 * The GPU's functions: the PCI children of the root port's devinfo
+	 * node (acpica tags PCI nodes with their ACPI device at boot). Their
+	 * vendor and class come from the properties the PCI enumerator set,
+	 * so this reads no config space until it has decided to act.
+	 */
+	if (acpica_get_devinfo(port, &pdip) != AE_OK || pdip == NULL) {
+		cmn_err(CE_NOTE, "tzmon: solnix-dgpu-off: %s has no devinfo "
+		    "node; nothing done", name);
+		return;
+	}
+	ndi_devi_enter(pdip);
+	for (cdip = ddi_get_child(pdip); cdip != NULL;
+	    cdip = ddi_get_next_sibling(cdip)) {
+		tzmon_dgpu_fn_t *f = &fn[nfn];
+		int ven;
+
+		if (acpica_get_bdf(cdip, &f->bus, &f->dev, &f->func) < 0)
+			continue;
+		if (nfn == TZMON_DGPU_MAXFN) {
+			ndi_devi_exit(pdip);
+			cmn_err(CE_NOTE, "tzmon: solnix-dgpu-off: %s has more "
+			    "than %d functions; nothing done", name,
+			    TZMON_DGPU_MAXFN);
+			return;
+		}
+		ven = ddi_prop_get_int(DDI_DEV_T_ANY, cdip, DDI_PROP_DONTPASS,
+		    "vendor-id", -1);
+		f->class = ddi_prop_get_int(DDI_DEV_T_ANY, cdip,
+		    DDI_PROP_DONTPASS, "class-code", -1);
+		f->drv = i_ddi_devi_attached(cdip) ? ddi_driver_name(cdip) :
+		    NULL;
+		f->dip = cdip;
+		if (ven == TZMON_DGPU_VENDOR && f->class != -1 &&
+		    ((f->class >> 16) & 0xff) == PCI_CLASS_DISPLAY)
+			nvdisp++;
+		if (cdip == fbdip) {
+			ndi_devi_exit(pdip);
+			cmn_err(CE_NOTE, "tzmon: solnix-dgpu-off: %s@%x,%x is "
+			    "the console; nothing done", ddi_node_name(cdip),
+			    f->dev, f->func);
+			return;
+		}
+		if (f->drv != NULL && !tzmon_dgpu_is_generic(f->drv)) {
+			ndi_devi_exit(pdip);
+			cmn_err(CE_NOTE, "tzmon: solnix-dgpu-off: %s@%x,%x has "
+			    "a driver (%s); nothing done", ddi_node_name(cdip),
+			    f->dev, f->func, f->drv);
+			return;
+		}
+		nfn++;
+	}
+	ndi_devi_exit(pdip);
+	if (nvdisp == 0) {
+		cmn_err(CE_NOTE, "tzmon: solnix-dgpu-off: %s has no NVIDIA "
+		    "display function (%d function(s)); nothing done", name,
+		    nfn);
+		return;
+	}
+
+	(void) acpica_eval_int(pr, "_STA", &sta0);
+	if (sta0 == 0) {
+		cmn_err(CE_NOTE, "tzmon: solnix-dgpu-off: %s _PR3 power "
+		    "resource already off (_STA 0); nothing done", name);
+		return;
+	}
+
+	/*
+	 * Offline every function first: that detaches vgatext/audiohd if
+	 * they attached, and keeps any driver from attaching later. A
+	 * function that will not go offline could still be in use and would
+	 * then touch a powered-off device: stop before any change, and put
+	 * back what was detached so the machine is as it was.
+	 */
+	for (i = 0; i < nfn; i++) {
+		if (ndi_devi_offline(fn[i].dip, 0) != NDI_SUCCESS) {
+			cmn_err(CE_NOTE, "tzmon: solnix-dgpu-off: %s@%x,%x "
+			    "(%s) would not go offline; GPU left powered",
+			    ddi_node_name(fn[i].dip), fn[i].dev, fn[i].func,
+			    fn[i].drv != NULL ? fn[i].drv : "no driver");
+			while (--i >= 0)
+				(void) ndi_devi_online(fn[i].dip, 0);
+			return;
+		}
+		if (fn[i].drv != NULL)
+			ndet++;
+	}
+	for (i = 0; i < nfn; i++)
+		d3[i] = tzmon_dgpu_d3hot(&fn[i]);
+
+	/* then the power resource; nothing touches the GPU after this */
+	(void) AcpiEvaluateObject(pr, "_OFF", NULL, NULL);
+	(void) acpica_eval_int(pr, "_STA", &sta1);
+
+	cmn_err(CE_NOTE, "tzmon: solnix-dgpu-off: %s: %d function(s) at "
+	    "bus %d dev %d offlined (%d driver(s) detached), PM state %d%s; "
+	    "_PR3 _OFF evaluated, _STA %d -> %d", name, nfn, fn[0].bus,
+	    fn[0].dev, ndet, d3[0], (d3[0] == PCI_PMCSR_D3HOT) ? " (D3hot)" :
+	    (d3[0] < 0 ? " (no PM capability)" : " (D3hot not reached)"),
+	    sta0, sta1);
+}
